          "case_name": "Diana H. v. Rubin",
          "citation": "217 Ariz. 131, 171 P.3d 200 (App. 2007)",
          "court": "Court of Appeals of Arizona",
          "year": 2007,
          "date_decided": "2007-11-21",
          "holding": "The court of appeals vacated the order authorizing the agency to consent to immunizations, holding that a dependency adjudication does not extinguish a parent's residual right to direct her child's religious upbringing and that the State had not shown a compelling interest overriding her religious objection.",
          "relevance": "The controlling Arizona case on the agency's authority to authorize medical care for a child in its custody over parental objection.",
          "quote": "the state's responsibility to provide medical care for a dependent child is expressly \"subject to\" a body of parental rights and duties retained by the parent",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2637228/diana-h-v-rubin/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 2637228
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Wallis ex rel. Wallis v. Spencer",
          "citation": "202 F.3d 1126 (9th Cir. 2000)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit",
          "year": 1999,
          "date_decided": "1999-09-14",
          "holding": "The Ninth Circuit reversed summary judgment for the city on the § 1983 claims, holding that absent risk of dissipating evidence or an urgent medical problem the state must notify parents and obtain judicial approval before subjecting children in protective custody to investigatory physical examinations, and that a jury must decide whether there was reasonable cause for the removal.",
          "relevance": "The leading circuit authority distinguishing urgent medical treatment from investigatory examinations of a child in state custody.",
          "quote": "The right to family association includes the right of parents to make important medical decisions for their children",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/7079922/wallis-ex-rel-wallis-v-spencer/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 7079922
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Momox-Caselis v. Donohue",
          "citation": "987 F.3d 835 (9th Cir. 2021)",
          "court": "United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit",
          "year": 2021,
          "date_decided": "2021-02-03",
          "holding": "The Ninth Circuit affirmed summary judgment for the county and its officials in a suit over a foster child's death, holding the family failed to prove deliberate indifference under the special-relationship exception or to establish a Monell claim given the county's licensing and training policies.",
          "relevance": "Addresses medication and caregiving failures in a licensed foster home as a substantive due process question.",
          "quote": "The \"special relationship\" exception applies when there is a custodial relationship between the plaintiff and the State, such that the State assumes some responsibility for the plaintiff's safety and well-being.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/4853292/sergio-momox-caselis-v-tara-donohue/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 4853292
        }
      ],
